  "notes": "Result: 10 of 10 rows are correct. 0 rows are imprecise. 0 rows are wrong. Method: for each name I ran git grep over the checkout (commit 7eddde7895 plus the staged files), read every read site and set site, followed the helper functions, and graded each sentence of the row against the code. I did not build or run repository code. One bash one-line check outside the repository confirmed the octal claims of the BUILD_ARTIFACT_MAX_AGE_DAYS row: 010 gives 8, and 08 stops bash 5.1 with an arithmetic error. Facts that the rows leave out, none of which changes a grade: (1) DICE_GRANT_TOKEN: the Dice daemon creates the token only in shared mode (bin/dice:3602). The wrappers remove the four grant variables before they start the program on a legacy host (bin/rinzler:309). The daemon also checks the user and the slots in a grant-check request (bin/dice:3128, bin/dice:3131). (2) TRON_INGEST_PLUGIN_BUNDLE_STAMP_REQUIRED: the sentence that a makefile assignment beats the environment holds for a normal make run. The make option -e reverses that order. (3) TRON_AMX_DISABLE: amx_available is also false on a CPU without AMX and in a build without TRON_AMX_DISPATCH. The AMX kernel also needs a full 64-token page and a bf16 executor (h/tron/kernels/amx_attn_iface.hpp:19). (4) TRON_ATTN_SECTION_SPLIT: a number that does not fit in 64 bits is invalid and aborts, it is not lowered to 16 (h/tron/models/model.hpp:148). Splitting has two more conditions: the section holds one page with at least 32 relevant queries, and the phase has at least 2 workers per page task (h/tron/models/model.hpp:3268, h/tron/models/model.hpp:3275). (5) BUILD_ARTIFACT_MAX_AGE_DAYS: a second pass of the script removes quarantine directories named .purge-<7 hex>-N-N at any age (bin/ci/ci-cleanup-build-artifacts.sh:86). The variable does not control that pass. (6) MFLAGS: the script removes the name only from its first four make commands, which are the warning check. The row says this in its last cell. (7) USE_PYTHON_TOKENIZER: the quoted warning also appears when the Python tokenizer is used for another reason (no tokenizer.json, or VALIDATE_TOKENIZERS)."
